      "id": 123729,
      "name": "Killswitch",
      "username": "Killswitch",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/killswitch/{size}/2116_2.png",
      "created_at": "2014-12-16T15:30:00.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"dshields\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/dshields/48/1968_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> dshields:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Hello All,I wanted to introduce myself, my name is Dennis. I got introduced to Sentinels of the Multiverse about 3 weeks ago and I was hooked. I have since then I have Purchased Sentinels of the Multiverse: Enhanced Edition, Rook City &amp; Infernal Relics, Shattered Timelines, and Vengeance. And have got all the Mini-Expansion Cards. I wanted to share my Storage Solution.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Welcome to the forums!</p>\n<p>I think this probably should go in its own thread, but while we're here I just wanted to say I really like your setup. I might consider picking up that storage box, it looks like it's got plenty of room for future sets, as well as dice, counters, oversize villians, etc.</p>\n<p>Do you think using the standard dividers would work well in that box?</p>",
