    {
      "id": 123730,
      "name": "dshields",
      "username": "dshields",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/dshields/{size}/1968_2.png",
      "created_at": "2014-12-16T17:22:23.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"xThe Killswitch\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n xThe Killswitch:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div><b>dshields wrote:</b><br><blockquote>Hello All,I wanted to introduce myself, my name is Dennis. I got introduced to Sentinels of the Multiverse about 3 weeks ago and I was hooked. I have since then I have Purchased Sentinels of the Multiverse: Enhanced Edition, Rook City &amp; Infernal Relics, Shattered Timelines, and Vengeance. And have got all the Mini-Expansion Cards. I wanted to share my Storage Solution.\n&nbsp;\n</blockquote></div>\nWelcome to the forums!I think this probably should go in its own thread, but while we're here I just wanted to say I really like your setup. I might consider picking up that storage box, it looks like it's got plenty of room for future sets, as well as dice, counters, oversize villians, etc.Do you think using the standard dividers would work well in that box?\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Since I used Spiff’s Boxes, even if you laid them down lengthwise you still can’t see the dividers. So they are not very effective.&nbsp; But if you don’t use Spiff’s Boxes then you can also put 2 of the Big game boxes (EE and Veng for example) Side by side and still have room left over for your extras. I didn’t show it but there is also a small mesh bag on the top perfect size for the Oversized cards.</p>",
