      "raw": "[quote=\"xThe Killswitch\"]\n\n&nbsp;\n<div class=\"bb-quote\"><b>dshields wrote:</b><br /><blockquote class=\"bb-quote-body\">Hello All,I wanted to introduce myself, my name is Dennis. I got introduced to Sentinels of the Multiverse about 3 weeks ago and I was hooked. I have since then I have Purchased Sentinels of the Multiverse: Enhanced Edition, Rook City &amp; Infernal Relics, Shattered Timelines, and Vengeance. And have got all the Mini-Expansion Cards. I wanted to share my Storage Solution.\n&nbsp;\n</blockquote></div>\nWelcome to the forums!I think this probably should go in its own thread, but while we&#39;re here I just wanted to say I really like your setup. I might consider picking up that storage box, it looks like it&#39;s got plenty of room for future sets, as well as dice, counters, oversize villians, etc.Do you think using the standard dividers would work well in that box?\n\n[/quote]\n\nSince I used Spiff&rsquo;s Boxes, even if you laid them down lengthwise you still can&rsquo;t see the dividers. So they are not very effective.&nbsp; But if you don&rsquo;t use Spiff&rsquo;s Boxes then you can also put 2 of the Big game boxes (EE and Veng for example) Side by side and still have room left over for your extras. I didn&rsquo;t show it but there is also a small mesh bag on the top perfect size for the Oversized cards.\n",
